# Project Evolution Plan & Comprehensive .todo Specification: Got You With My Telegram (v3.0)

## Completed Tasks (v2.0 Stable)
- [x] Standardize script and project naming (`got-you-with-my-telegram.py`).
- [x] Add robust exception handling and request timeouts for network operations.
- [x] Create comprehensive unit test suite (`tests/test_got_you_with_my_telegram.py`) achieving >90% test coverage.
- [x] Fix Python 3.12+ / 3.14 `asyncio.get_child_watcher` compatibility.
- [x] Add root privilege check and `tshark` capture initialization error handling.
- [x] Implement optional IP-API Pro API key configuration with first-run validation and freeware endpoint default fallback (with `X-Rl` and `X-Ttl` rate limit header tracking).
- [x] Resolve local/private IP range mapping by querying public IP while preserving local IP display.
- [x] Filter out local interface IPs and WAN IPs to exclusively track the remote interlocutor (call answerer).
- [x] **Telegram Geolocation Heuristics:** Integrated Telegram metadata and signaling packet profiling to assist location identification.
- [x] **Interactive Startup Menu Options:** Implemented menu prompt system supporting [1] Simple Location Tracking, [2] Triangle Tracking (5+ min telemetry with Ctrl+C safe dump), and [3] Forensic Audio Recording (`.wav` audio stream capture in background).
- [x] **TraceRoute & Network Hop Analysis:** Added real-time network hop visualization and traceroute diagnostics targeting the remote call answerer.
- [x] **Strict Target Isolation:** Guaranteed that all recorded telemetry, geolocation results, audio captures, and traceroute outputs focus exclusively on the target call answerer and never leak data from the caller's host machine.

